{:event/id "fbf47208-46a1-4b27-960b-b411c6f840ea" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:a36c7aed-cf49-4fbf-a94e-826d672bd45a" :event/seq 1 :event/causes ["a36c7aed-cf49-4fbf-a94e-826d672bd45a"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:a36c7aed-cf49-4fbf-a94e-826d672bd45a" :event/at "2026-09-08T14:15:10Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/action-execution-is-prioritized-resolution-ladder :finding/shapes #{:dispatch-table :multimethod :resolver :resource} :finding/current-name "knoxx.backend.domain.action.interpreter/execute! -> katamorph.action.interpreter/execute!" :finding/candidate-name "ActionResolutionLadder<Invocation,Registry,Resource>" :finding/claim "Action execution has an explicit precedence law. An inline :action/fn compiles and executes before any registered implementation; absent an inline function, a currently registered :action/kind executes before EDN resource lookup; only when the kind is not registered may an enabled action resource matched by :action/id or :resource/qualified-id rewrite the invocation; unresolved requests finally fall through to the host run-action! capability. A matching resource therefore does not have equal authority with a registered handler, and this is an ordered domain-resolution algorithm rather than one generic registry abstraction."}}
{:event/id "16278088-f5b0-4c98-9e55-eedfbfd602dc" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:a36c7aed-cf49-4fbf-a94e-826d672bd45a" :event/seq 2 :event/causes ["fbf47208-46a1-4b27-960b-b411c6f840ea"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:a36c7aed-cf49-4fbf-a94e-826d672bd45a" :event/at "2026-09-08T14:15:10Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/action-resource-expansion-is-bounded-asymmetric-overlay :finding/shapes #{:resource :facet :projection :resolver} :finding/current-name "katamorph.action.interpreter/action-resource + expand-action-resource + redirects" :finding/candidate-name "BoundedActionExpansion<Reference,Definition>" :finding/claim "EDN action-resource indirection is bounded to one expansion by the default redirect budget. Expansion replaces the reference :action/kind with the resource kind and merges resource :action/with defaults underneath invocation :action/with, so call-site argument values win. In contrast, a resource-defined :action/scope or :action/fn is associated after that merge and therefore replaces the corresponding invocation facet. This field-sensitive precedence and bounded dereference law is materially narrower than a generic recursive resolver or map overlay; Knoxx tests pin kind replacement and caller-over-resource :action/with precedence."}}
{:event/id "4275d088-c808-427b-bf97-7f89ff494851" :event/schema {:schema/root "8eb19ab0e4b70e205a84a627fd3e15c3ba79c0fd8c792d37e72f3c79511e0bf9" :schema/id :archaeology/finding-recorded :schema/hash "f2ad682fa2ac851a5d18b436849d3c59f07eb5f9ebe6179d231d7254b8d89848"} :event/type :archaeology/finding-recorded :event/stream "archaeology:findings:a36c7aed-cf49-4fbf-a94e-826d672bd45a" :event/seq 3 :event/causes ["16278088-f5b0-4c98-9e55-eedfbfd602dc"] :event/actor "agent:chatgpt" :event/subject "archaeology:a36c7aed-cf49-4fbf-a94e-826d672bd45a" :event/at "2026-09-08T14:15:10Z" :event/data {:finding/id :knoxx/katamorph-boundary-is-explicit-capability-port :finding/shapes #{:protocol :adapter :resource :scope} :finding/current-name "contract-runtime-deps/build-deps + Knoxx action-interpreter compatibility wrapper" :finding/candidate-name "ContractRuntimePort<Host,Runtime>" :finding/claim "Knoxx's action interpreter wrapper owns no execution algorithm; it delegates directly to Katamorph. Knoxx instead injects a :contract-runtime/deps capability map supplying action execution and lookup, scope declarations, filters, stores, and resource lookup. The reusable runtime therefore owns resolution semantics while the host owns concrete capabilities and deployment integration. This is a protocol/capability boundary expressed through injected functions, not another executable registry or domain algorithm."}}
